<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Balance Druid DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from Phase 2 raids and crafted gear.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Balance Druid DPS Phase 2</h2>In phase 2, Balance will be much closer to meeting all of our soft stat caps. You should always aim to meet the required Hit rating. If you are fully talented into <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33596/balance-of-power">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_balanceofpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Balance of Power</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33602/improved-faerie-fire">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Improved Faerie Fire</span></a>, you only need 10% Hit from gear (263 rating) to reach the hit cap requirement for a boss fight. Furthermore, if you play for the Alliance, Draenei provide <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=28878/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a> to their party members, bringing your required Hit to 9% (237 rating).<br/>
<br/>Crit continues to be a very strong stat for Balance. In Phase 2, we will be getting a lot more of it which will further alleviate any mana issues, as well as smooth out our rotation through eclipse procs. In some setups, you will reach the crit soft-cap using buffs like <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=54648/focus-magic">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_studentofmagic.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Focus Magic</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>2 piece Tier 8 is a large boost to damage while in an eclipse state. 4 piece, while counterintuitive is not the strongest on single target "patchwork-Esque fights," but for fights with lots of movement and/<wbr/>or multiple targets, 4 piece is the way to go. There will be quite a few of these high-movement fights in Ulduar.<br/>
<br/>These sets assume you have access to Engineering but leave the second profession open. For more information on other options for individual slots, read the sections below.<br/>
<br/>There are 3 tabs listed below. One for Horde/<wbr/>alliance without a Draenei, one with a Draenei in your party, and one for high mobility and cleave fights that uses 4pc Tier 8.<br/>
